[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m You then asked me “Why not do the GEMM in Triton?”, correct. Because GEMM (GEMM) is not an elementwise operation; it’s a dense matrix multiplication, often best handled by cuBLAS/cublas-like routines and libraries like cuBLAS or PyTorch matmul. A custom Triton kernel for GEMM (matmul) will not beat cuBLLOCK; you would need 1–2 orders of magnitude effort to be competitive with vendor libraries.
