[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - We want C = A^T @ B, with A shape (K, M), B shape (K, N), C shape (M, N).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Equivalent to a standard matmul C = A’ @ B’ where A’=(M,K) is A transposed, B’=(K,N) is B as-is. But transposing A to a contiguous (M,K) would cost a big copy (M*K ≈ 16.7M elements), which is often worse than paying for non-unit stride loads in the kernel.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Better: keep A as (K,M) and index it as A(k, i) when we need A’(i, k). Same for B: keep as (K,N) and index B(k, j).
