[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Memory layout:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - A is (K,M): strides (sA_k, sA_m). Typically contiguous in M (last dim), so sA_m=1, sA_k=M.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - B is (K,N): strides (sB_k, sB_n). Typically contiguous in N, so sB_n=1, sB_k=N.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Loads will be strided along K dimension: step size sA_k or sB_k which could be large (e.g., M=2048 → sA_k=2048). That’s not ideal but acceptable if K is the loop dimension and we keep BLOCK_K reasonably small to improve locality.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Alternative would be to make A’ = A.T (contiguous (M,K)) to get unit stride on A, but that copy is expensive. Given K is the loop dimension, strided loads along K are the price we pay to avoid the copy.
