[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Observations:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - torch.cumsum on GPU is already pretty optimized and may use vendor libraries or highly tuned kernels.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - However, writing a custom Triton kernel gives control and can be competitive, especially if we tailor memory access and parallelism to the shape.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - The operation is a prefix sum (scan) along one axis. It is sequential dependency-wise per row, but we can parallelize across rows and blocks of columns.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Constraints and goals:
