[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 1) Restate the original operation
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - The PyTorch forward computes torch.matmul(A.T, B) with:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - A shape (K, M)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - B shape (K, N)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Result C shape (M, N), with C = A.T @ B
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Elementwise: C[i, j] = sum over k of A[k, i] * B[k, j].
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 2) Why Triton can help
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - We can implement a blocked matmul kernel that:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Does not materialize A.T, but indexes A using its original strides as A[k, i].
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Uses tiling for good cache reuse and memory coalescing.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Accumulates in float32 for numerical stability (especially for fp16/bf16).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - For specific sizes and mixed precision, custom kernels can match or beat generic libraries.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 3) Kernel design
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Tile sizes BLOCK_M x BLOCK_N x BLOCK_K.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Grid over (M, N): programs = (ceil_div(M, BM), ceil_div(N, BN)).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Loop over K in steps of BK:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Load A tile of shape (BM, BK): ptr A + k*sA0 + i*sA1.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Load B tile of shape (BK, BN): ptr B + k*sB0 + j*sB1.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - acc += dot(a, b) with fp32 accumulation.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Store acc to C with proper masking.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
