[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Lesson: always provide a real kernel so the code does not fall back and allocate a second full tensor.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m Design for a correct and fast-enough kernel
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Map one Triton program to one row.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Process the row in fixed-size tiles of BLOCK elements (power of two, e.g., 1024).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - For each tile:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Load tile into registers (with mask for tail).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Compute inclusive scan within the tile用 Hillis–Steele: O(log BLOCK) vector ops.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Add a per-row carry (from previous tiles) to all positions before scan so the scan result is correctly offset across tiles.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Store results.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Update carry = last valid element of this tile.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - This achieves:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Each element loaded once, stored once.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - O(N log BLOCK) vector ops total (fast).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Correctness details:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Out-of-bounds lanes are zero; zeros don’t change cumsum of in-bounds values.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   -carry propagation ensures continuity across tiles.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m Triton specifics and tricky part: in-register right-shift
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Hillis–Steele needs v shifted right by 2^d at each step.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Direct vector indexing vals[idx] is not allowed in Triton for arbitrary idx.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - But we can implement the shift legally and efficiently by constructing the shifted vector s without reading memory:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - s[l] = (l >= shift) ? vals[l - shift] : 0
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - We cannot index vals[l - shift] directly, but we can observe that after the previous iteration, vals[l] already contains the sum of all previous elements within the tile. So we can construct s by using vals itself arithmetically:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     - Define s_tmp = where(cols >= shift, vals, 0)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     - Then s = s_tmp - where(cols >= 2*shift, vals, 0)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m       - Reason: s_tmp has v[l-shift] at position l only when l>=shift; subtracting the vals at position l when l>=2*shift removes the v[l-2*shift] component, and so on, producing the pure shifted component for this step.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     - This is a vector operation, no memory gathers, and respects dependencies.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Then v = v + s accomplishes v += v shifted by 2^d.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m Edge cases and safeguards
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Only optimize 2D, dim=1 on CUDA; fallback otherwise.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Enforce contiguous for simplicity.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Dtypes: float32 recommended; half/bfloat16 should work.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - BLOCK must be power-of-two <= N.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m Tuning
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - BLOCK=1024, num_warps=4 is a good start on B200.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Could go 2048 for fewer tiles, but 1024 is safer w.r.t. register pressure.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m Final code: Triton kernel with correct in-register scan and ModelNew entry point
