[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m Key observations
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - The residual is applied after the final 1x1 projection. That means you are adding the input (shape [B, Cin, H, W]) to the output (shape [B, Cout, H’, W’]). This will only make mathematical sense if Cin == Cout and H’==H, W’==W and stride==1. Most MBConv implementations apply the residual before the final projection (right after depthwise), but the given code applies it after. I will preserve this behavior for correctness parity.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m Where Triton can help
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - cuDNN’s Conv2d is already highly optimized. Re-implementing convolution in Triton to beat cuDNN is non-trivial and lengthy.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - The biggest easy wins here are fusing simple elementwise chains and small fixed-kernel ops:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - 1x1 Conv2d is a GEMM per (b, h, w) location: Y[b, oc, h, w] = sum_ic X[b, ic, h, w] * W[oc, ic]. This maps nicely to a small Triton kernel.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Depthwise Conv2d with kernel KxK is also amenable: for each (b, c, h, w) you do sum over kh,kw of X[b, c, h+kh, w+kw] * W[c, kh, kw]. You can write a kernel that loops over kh,kw and accumulates in registers.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Fusing ReLU6 into the convolution kernels saves an extra pass over memory.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m Plan
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Replace expand 1x1 + BN + ReLU6 with a single Triton kernel that computes expand 1x1 (GEMM) and applies ReLU6 in-register.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Replace depthwise + BN + ReLU6 with a single Triton kernel that computes depthwise conv and applies ReLU6.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Keep project 1x1 + BN as standard Conv2d + BN (fast path via cuDNN).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Keep the post-project residual addition in PyTorch: it’s a single elementwise add; not a big win to move to Triton for this specific case.
