[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m Notes
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - This kernel fixes the previous indexing and accumulation bugs.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - It uses true 5D strides, so it works with standard NCDHW layouts after .contiguous().
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - It computes softmax in float32 for numerical stability, adds bias before softmax, applies tanh, and scales— all in a single pass over memory for storage (three logical passes over channels but only one store pass).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - If Triton is unavailable or the tensor is on CPU, it falls back to the original PyTorch implementation for correctness.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m Potential further improvements
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - If you can accept a tiny numerical difference, you could approximate tanh to save time, but that’s usually not worth it.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - You could experiment with num_warps/num_stages and BLOCK_C for your specific shapes.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Advanced: fuse the mean over depth into the same kernel by looping over D and accumulating, but that’s a larger change and not necessary to get a clear speedup here. 
