[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Support float16/bfloat16 inputs with float32 accumulation to leverage tensor cores (you’d need to carefully manage dtypes and possibly use mixed-precision).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - If you know tensors are contiguous, you can specialize strides for coalesced loads (e.g., sBN=1) and choose BLOCK_N to maximize vectorized memory transactions. 
