[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 1) Restating the original operation
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - The PyTorch forward returns torch.matmul(A.T, B).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Given:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - A: shape (K, M)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - B: shape (K, N)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - So A.T: shape (M, K), and C = A.T @ B yields shape (M, N).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Element-wise: C[i, j] = sum over k of A.T[i, k] * B[k, j] = sum over k of A[k, i] * B[k, j].
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 2) Where Triton can help
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - torch.matmul on CUDA uses cuBLAS, which is extremely optimized. For many sizes, it’s hard to beat.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - However, a custom Triton kernel can:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Avoid materializing A.T by indexing A with its strides as if it were (M, K).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Fuse the operation into a single pass with tiling over M, N, and K.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Control block sizes and warps to suit the problem.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 3) Root cause of the previous failure and fix
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - The compilation error: “int32[] used as tl.static_range end value is not a constexpr” arose because tl.static_range requires a compile-time constant, but K was passed as a runtime argument.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Fix: Remove tl.static_range and use a dynamic while loop over K with step BLOCK_K. This is the standard pattern in Triton for GEMM kernels when K is not known at compile time.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 4) Kernel design
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Treat problem as C = A @ B with logical shapes:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - A: (M, K), storage is original (K, M); index A[m, k] -> A storage at (k, m). Use strides sAM = A.stride(1), sAK = A.stride(0).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - B: (K, N), storage is (K, N); strides sBK = B.stride(0), sBN = B.stride(1).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - C: (M, N), contiguous or strided; we’ll use its strides sCM, sCN.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Tiling:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Each program computes a BLOCK_M x BLOCK_N tile of C.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Loop k from 0 to K (step BLOCK_K): load A tile (BM x BK) and B tile (BK x BN), acc += dot(A_tile, B_tile).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Memory:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - A loads are strided along K due to (K, M) storage; acceptable.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - B loads are contiguous along N (sBN = 1); along K is stride sBK.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Dtype:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Use float32 throughout to match torch.rand default.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 5) Launch configuration
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - BLOCK_M = 128, BLOCK_N = 128, BLOCK_K = 32 as a reasonable starting point.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - num_warps = 4, num_stages = 3.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Grid = (ceil_div(M, BLOCK_M), ceil_div(N, BLOCK_N)).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 6) Correctness and robustness
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Validate shapes.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - If tensors are not CUDA or not float32, fall back to torch.matmul.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Support arbitrary strides via stride parameters.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Masks for edge tiles.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 7) Performance considerations
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - For the given sizes (M=4096, K=8192, N=8192), this is a large GEMM. cuBLAS is very strong; a hand-rolled kernel may or may not be faster. The main value here is correctness and demonstrating Triton usage.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Possible future tuning: autotune block sizes, use BLOCK_K=64/128, num_warps=8, support fp16/bf16 with fp32 accumulation to use tensor cores.
