[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 1) What the original PyTorch code does
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - The forward computes torch.matmul(A.T, B).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - With shapes:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - A is (K, M)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - B is (K, N)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - A.T is (M, K)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Result is (M, N), with formula C[i, j] = sum over k of A.T[i, k] * B[k, j].
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Interpreting indices:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - A.T[i, k] = A[k, i]
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - B[k, j] = B[j, k]
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - So C[i, j] = sum_k A[k, i] * B[j, k]
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - This is not the standard GEMM C = A @ B = (M, K) @ (K, N) = (M, N).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - It’s a bit unusual because the first operand is A^T (shape M x K) while typical is A shape M x K. Regardless, we must match this exact operation.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 2) Computational complexity and memory access
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - C is size M x N; K is the reduction dimension.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Arithmetic: ~M*N*K multiplications/additions.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - For the provided sizes (M=2048, K=8192, N=4096), that’s about 1.37e11 MACs ≈ 2.7e10 FLOPs if FP32.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Memory:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - A is (K, M) contiguous in M for a fixed K row.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - B is (K, N) contiguous in N for a fixed K row.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - We will read A[k, i] and B[j, k]; both are contiguous along their second dim when fixing k. Good for coalesced loads if we tile along i and j.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 3) Why Triton can help
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - torch.matmul routes to cuBLAS which is extremely optimized (TF32/tensor cores, advanced blocking, scheduling).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - A custom Triton kernel can:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Match the exact operation layout without transposes or extra copies.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Use tiling and shared reuse to suit the specific shapes.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Potentially fuse or specialize for half/bfloat16 to use tensor cores (but that requires changing math to matmul in low precision; here we must preserve dtype).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Caveat: For pure FP32 GEMM, cuBLAS will often be faster unless we use very shape-specialized kernels or mixed precision. Still, a well-written Triton kernel is a good teaching example and can be competitive for some shapes.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 4) Kernel design
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Compute C = A^T @ B, where:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - A is (K, M)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - B is (K, N)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - C is (M, N)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - We will tile:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - BLOCK_M along i (rows of C / cols of A^T)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - BLOCK_N along j (cols of C)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - BLOCK_K along k (reduction)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Each program instance computes a submatrix C[offs_m : offs_m+BM, offs_n : offs_n+BN].
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Loop over K in steps of BK:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Load A_block of shape (BK, BM): indices (k + offs_k, i + offs_m)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Load B_block of shape (BK, BN): indices (j + offs_n, k + offs_k)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Accumulate acc += dot(A_block, B_block) -> shape (BM, BN)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - After loop, store acc to C.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Memory strides:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - A is (K, M): strides (sA0 = M, sA1 = 1) if contiguous; generally sA0 = A.stride(0), sA1 = A.stride(1).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - B is (K, N): strides (sB0 = N, sB1 = 1) if contiguous.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - C is (M, N): strides (sC0 = N, sC1 = 1) if contiguous.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - We will pass strides to be safe with non-contiguous too (but get_inputs creates contiguous).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Data types:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Start with float32 to keep it simple and numerically stable.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Could be extended to float16/bfloat16 with accumulation in float32.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 5) Tiling and launch parameters
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - BLOCK sizes:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - 64/128 are common starting points.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Given M, N, K are large, 128x128x32 is a decent starting tile.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - num_warps/num_stages:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - num_warps: 4–8 is typical; 4 or 8 are good.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - num_stages: 2–4 to pipeline loads.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Grid:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - (ceil_div(M, BM), ceil_div(N, BN))
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 6) Correctness and numerical considerations
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - The formula matches torch.matmul(A.T, B).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - FP32 should match PyTorch closely; small differences possible due to different reduction order.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - If you need bitwise equality, that’s rarely guaranteed vs cuBLAS, but close within tolerance is.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 7) Fallback and device
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - If tensors are on CPU, fall back to torch.matmul.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - If on CUDA, run Triton.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Ensure contiguous for simplicity; otherwise pass strides (we’ll pass strides anyway).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 8) Extensions (not implemented here to keep it clear)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Mixed-precision: cast to fp16/bf16, use tensor cores, accumulate fp32.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Autotune: multiple (BM, BN, BK) configs with triton.autotune.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Grouped matmul schedule, double-buffering, and more advanced pipelining.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m Triton implementation: ModelNew
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m Below is a Triton-based implementation that computes C = A^T @ B with the same semantics as torch.matmul(A.T, B). It uses tiling and a simple loop over K. It assumes float32 tensors on CUDA; falls back to torch if not.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m ```python
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m import math
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m import torch
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m import torch.nn as nn
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m import triton
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m import triton.language as tl
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m @triton.jit
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m def _matmul_at_b_kernel(
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     A, B, C,
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     M, N, K,
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     sA0, sA1,  # strides for A (K, M)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     sB0, sB1,  # strides for B (K, N)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     sC0, sC1,  # strides for C (M, N)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     BLOCK_M: tl.constexpr,
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     BLOCK_N: tl.constexpr,
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     BLOCK_K: tl.constexpr,
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m ):
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     # Program ids
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     pid_m = tl.program_id(0)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     pid_n = tl.program_id(1)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     # Offsets for the output tile we compute
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     offs_m = pid_m * BLOCK_M + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_M)    # [BM]
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     offs_n = pid_n * BLOCK_N + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_N)    # [BN]
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     # accumulator in fp32
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     acc = tl.zeros((BLOCK_M, BLOCK_N), dtype=tl.float32)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     # loop over K dimension
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     for k0 in range(0, K, BLOCK_K):
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         offs_k = k0 + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_K)  # [BK]
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         # Pointers for A block: shape (BK, BM)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         # A is (K, M): index A[k, i]
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         a_ptrs = A + (offs_k[:, None] * sA0) + (offs_m[None, :] * sA1)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         # Pointers for B block: shape (BK, BN)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         # B is (K, N): index B[j, k]
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         b_ptrs = B + (offs_n[None, :] * sB1) + (offs_k[:, None] * sB0)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         # Masks to guard out-of-bounds
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         a_mask = (offs_k[:, None] < K) & (offs_m[None, :] < M)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         b_mask = (offs_n[None, :] < N) & (offs_k[:, None] < K)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         # Load with masks; 'other=0.0' is fine since we'll sum and mask doesn't let OOB contribute
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         a = tl.load(a_ptrs, mask=a_mask, other=0.0)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         b = tl.load(b_ptrs, mask=b_mask, other=0.0)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         # Accumulate
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         acc += tl.dot(a, b)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     # Store result to C: C[i, j] = acc
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     c_ptrs = C + (offs_m[:, None] * sC0) + (offs_n[None, :] * sC1)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     c_mask = (offs_m[:, None] < M) & (offs_n[None, :] < N)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     tl.store(c_ptrs, acc, mask=c_mask)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m class ModelNew(nn.Module):
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     def __init__(self):
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         super(ModelNew, self).__init__()
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     def forward(self, A: torch.Tensor, B: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         """
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         Computes torch.matmul(A.T, B) via a Triton kernel.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         Shapes:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m           A: (K, M)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m           B: (K, N)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         Returns:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m           C: (M, N)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         """
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         # Fallback to PyTorch if not on CUDA
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         if not A.is_cuda or not B.is_cuda:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m             return torch.matmul(A.T, B)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         assert A.dim() == 2 and B.dim() == 2, f"Expected 2D tensors, got {A.shape}, {B.shape}"
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         K_A, M = A.shape
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         K_B, N = B.shape
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         assert K_A == K_B, f"Incompatible K dims: {K_A} vs {K_B}"
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         K = K_A
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         # Dtype: start with float32
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         if A.dtype != torch.float32 or B.dtype != torch.float32:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m             # Fallback for non-fp32 to keep it simple and correct
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m             return torch.matmul(A.T, B)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         # Allocate output
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         C = torch.empty((M, N), device=A.device, dtype=A.dtype)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         # Strides (in elements)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         sA0, sA1 = A.stride(0), A.stride(1)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         sB0, sB1 = B.stride(0), B.stride(1)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         sC0, sC1 = C.stride(0), C.stride(1)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         # Tile sizes (can be tuned)
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         BLOCK_M = 128
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         BLOCK_N = 128
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         BLOCK_K = 32
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         grid = (triton.cdiv(M, BLOCK_M), triton.cdiv(N, BLOCK_N))
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         _matmul_at_b_kernel[grid](
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m             A, B, C,
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m             M, N, K,
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m             sA0, sA1,
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m             sB0, sB1,
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m             sC0, sC1,
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m             BLOCK_M=BLOCK_M,
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m             BLOCK_N=BLOCK_N,
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m             BLOCK_K=BLOCK_K,
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m             num_warps=4,   # tuning knob
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m             num_stages=3,  # tuning knob
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         )
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m         return C
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
