[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Where Triton helps most:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - The sequence add → softmax → tanh → scale is multiple memory passes and kernel launches. Fusing them into a single kernel that operates per (b, h, w) position over channels C can reduce memory traffic and launch overhead substantially.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - We can compute a numerically stable softmax (max-sub, exp, sum, divide) and then apply tanh and scaling in the same pass over registers.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Root cause of prior issues and fixes:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Previous crash was due to using triton.language APIs not present (tanh). Fixed by removing tanh dependency and implementing tanh via exp identity inside the kernel.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Previous submission was flagged as a decoy kernel because the Triton kernel wasn’t actually used in the core computation path. This time, the fused kernel is integrated and invoked from ModelNew.forward on CUDA.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Kernel design:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Layout after mean: [B, C, 1, H, W]; we view as [B, C, H, W] contiguous.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Grid: 2D -> (B*H*W, ceil_div(C, BLOCK_C)).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Each program handles one (b, h, w) and a block of channels BLOCK_C.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Three passes over the channel block:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     1) Compute block max over valid channels.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     2) Compute sum of exp(x - max).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m     3) Normalize to prob = exp / sum, then tanh(prob) = (e^(2p) - 1) / (e^(2p) + 1), then scale, store.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Use masks for tail channels; invalidate invalid lanes by setting x = -inf so they don’t affect max/sum.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Numerical stability:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Softmax computed in float32 with max-sub trick.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Tanh implemented as (exp(2p) - 1) / (exp(2p) + 1); this is stable for p in [0,1].
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Compute in float32; cast back to input dtype at the end.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Performance considerations:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - BLOCK_C=128, num_warps=4 is a good starting point for C≈64–512.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Coalesced memory: indexing is contiguous over (H*W).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - Fusing ops saves passes over memory compared to separate PyTorch kernels.
