[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m What changed and why it fixes the issue
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - The kernel now computes exactly C = (A.T) @ B given A:(K,M) and B:(K,N), by viewing A as (M,K) via index mapping A[m,k] = A_orig[k,m] and keeping B as (K,N).
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - This removes the previous bug where I computed A @ B instead of A.T @ B.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - All other aspects (tiling, masking, strides) remain sound for float32.
