[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m Performance notes and tuning
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - BLOCK_M=128, BLOCK_N=128, BLOCK_K=32, num_warps=4, num_stages=2 is a solid starting point on B200 for these sizes. You can experiment with:
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - BLOCK_K=64 for higher compute intensity per tile.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m   - num_warps=8 for larger tiles.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - If you need half or bfloat16, you can extend the kernel to load in fp16/bf16 and accumulate in fp32 for more speed, but that requires careful casting in tl.dot.
