[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m 2) Where Triton can help and where it may not
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - ConvTranspose3d: keep using PyTorch/cuDNN.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Mean over depth: write a Triton kernel that, for each (b, c, h, w), loops over D and accumulates in float32, then stores one value. Memory access is simple and contiguous over D for typical layouts.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Softmax: write a Triton kernel that, for each (b, h, w), loads C values, does numerically stable softmax, stores C values. C=64 is small; one program per (b,h,w) is fine.
[36m(MultiTurnAsyncvLLMEngine pid=1400823)[0m - Tanh and scale: either do in PyTorch (cheap) or fold into softmax kernel (slightly fewer launches). I’ll keep them separate for clarity but they’re negligible.
