[36m(main_task pid=1372105)[0m Notes on correctness and numerical behavior
[36m(main_task pid=1372105)[0m - The kernel computes exactly C = A^T @ B using block tiling and fp32 accumulation. For float32 inputs, results should match torch.matmul closely (tiny numerical differences are possible due to different reduction orders).
[36m(main_task pid=1372105)[0m - For float16/bfloat16 inputs, we accumulate in fp32 and store in the requested output dtype, which is a common practice to improve numerical stability.
