[36m(main_task pid=1372105)[0m Performance considerations
[36m(main_task pid=1372105)[0m - cuBLAS is highly optimized; for many shapes it may outperform custom kernels. The Triton kernel here is meant to demonstrate fusion and control over tiling without materializing transposes.
[36m(main_task pid=1372105)[0m - You can tune BLOCK_M, BLOCK_N, BLOCK_K, num_warps, and num_stages for your GPU and problem size. Larger tiles (e.g., 128x128x32) and num_warps=8 may help on some architectures.
[36m(main_task pid=1372105)[0m - If M, N, K are small, the PyTorch fallback may be faster due to lower launch overhead.
